  'melon-trains':'Research, prototypes, and testing formed part of the four-week redesign. Bringing both journeys into one comparison meant people could see real-time fares, return ticket choices, and SplitSave options before committing to a booking.',
  'everkind':'The work moved from defining an initial conversation experience to connecting writing and chat. Journaling became part of V2 rather than the starting brief, giving the app a new way to support reflection alongside the companion.',
  'rhode-island-school-of-design':'Stakeholder workshops, user interviews, and prototype reviews shaped that direction. Reusable patterns carried the new identity across expressive public pages and practical student resources, with room for each to serve a different purpose.',
  'melon-flight':'The result layout groups route, timing, and price for comparison. Expanded details keep the journey in context, while fare information makes the differences between ticket options easier to inspect before checkout.',
  'melon-checkout':'The flow gives traveller and loyalty information a defined place, surfaces company-policy requirements, and brings the trip together for review before the final commitment. After booking, the itinerary and follow-up actions live together.',
  'qatar-2022':'Official tournament typography, photography, and colours set the visual direction. Culture, destinations, travel information, and stadium storytelling connected the excitement of the event with the practical details of a visit.',
  'design-labs':'We explored how people contribute to online communities, then combined AI-assisted categorisation with search by project, location, and skill. The MVP secured funding to develop the direction as a white-label platform.',
  'university-of-mary-washington':'Moodboards developed with Mindpower established the visual direction. Audience routes and wireframes shaped the content hierarchy, while a programme finder supported discovery across more than 60 majors and programmes. Reusable WordPress Block Editor components gave editors a consistent way to build and update pages.',
  'control-social':'I used the week to experiment with typography, feed layouts, reactions, and comments. The screens show a visual direction, not a tested product or a claim about audience engagement.',
  'pantrx':'I organised the concept around shared meals and weekly preparation. Progress indicators and pantry alerts explored how to show what was ready and what still needed attention. The result is a proof of concept for coordinating shopping, rather than a validated product.',
  'georgia-department-of-agriculture':'Clearer divisions and service routes gave the content structure. The visual direction reflected Georgia’s identity, while simpler forms and more scannable articles supported self-service. Reusable components helped the team create and update pages consistently.',
